{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "072S", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-smooth}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:315ce663dea25e3df0465f2f4c8102218b9295403cb83ccd91afde88712c73c3", "source_text": "A smooth cover", "source_text_hash": "sha256:55fa4c84aa4c7f8c0e49953eb8ab34feecc173a76f4dfd4e4d2fedd89058ff49", "unit_id": "tag:072S:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "072S", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}$", "MATH_0002": "$$\nW = \\Spec(\\mathbf{Z}[a_1, a_2, a_3, a_4, a_6, 1/\\Delta])\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta \\in \\mathbf{Z}[a_1, a_2, a_3, a_4, a_6]$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\mathbf{P}_W^2 \\supset E_W :\nzy^2 + a_1 xyz + a_3 yz^2 = x^3 + a_2x^2z + a_4xz^2 + a_6z^3.\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$f_W : E_W \\to W$", "MATH_0006": "$0_W : W \\to E_W$", "MATH_0007": "$f_W$", "MATH_0008": "$(0 : 1 : 0)$", "MATH_0009": "$12$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0011": "$a_i$", "MATH_0012": "$\\deg(a_i) = i$", "MATH_0013": "$E_W \\to W$", "MATH_0014": "\\begin{align*}\n\\Delta & = -a_6a_1^6 + a_4a_3a_1^5 + ((-a_3^2 - 12a_6)a_2 + a_4^2)a_1^4 + \\\\\n& (8a_4a_3a_2 + (a_3^3 + 36a_6a_3))a_1^3 + \\\\\n& ((-8a_3^2 - 48a_6)a_2^2 + 8a_4^2a_2 + (-30a_4a_3^2 + 72a_6a_4))a_1^2 + \\\\\n& (16a_4a_3a_2^2 + (36a_3^3 + 144a_6a_3)a_2 - 96a_4^2a_3)a_1 + \\\\\n& (-16a_3^2 - 64a_6)a_2^3 + 16a_4^2a_2^2 + (72a_4a_3^2 + 288a_6a_4)a_2 + \\\\\n& -27a_3^4 - 216a_6a_3^2  -64a_4^3 - 432a_6^2\n\\end{align*}", "MATH_0015": "$y^2 = x^3 + Ax + B$", "MATH_0016": "$-64A^3 - 432B^2 = -16(4A^3 + 27B^2)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c15be5605e27f9f4a60c689372e3c80143839414fceba580d3a5b0eac8ae8c1e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b50c61aa767f450aca148159a57df889eef77e4ada764c360eafbde2b5387be0", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe last thing we have to do is find a smooth cover of <MATH_0001>.\nIn fact, in some sense the existence of a smooth cover\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>implies<TEXTITCLOSE_0001><FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>This is a bit of a cheat because\nin checking the smoothness you have to prove something close to\nthe key fact -- after all smoothness is defined in terms of\nfibre products. The advantage is that you only have to prove the existence\nof these fibre products in the case that on one side you have the morphism\nthat you are trying to show provides the smooth cover.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001> the key fact!\nIn the case of elliptic curves we use the Weierstrass equation to\nconstruct one.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nSet\n<MATH_0002>\nwhere <MATH_0003> is a certain\npolynomial (see below). Set\n<MATH_0004>\nDenote <MATH_0005> the projection. Finally, denote <MATH_0006>\nthe section of <MATH_0007> given by <MATH_0008>. It turns out that\nthere is a degree <MATH_0009> homogeneous polynomial <MATH_0010> in <MATH_0011>\nwhere <MATH_0012> such that <MATH_0013> is smooth.\nYou can find it explicitly by computing partials of the\nWeierstrass equation -- of course you can also look it up. You can\nalso use pari/gp to compute it for you. Here it is\n<MATH_0014>\nYou may recognize the last two terms from the case\n<MATH_0015> having discriminant <MATH_0016>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a37d57246ba976c6923b7ec8775e2cdd1578262dcc61ca63d377ff7b6087a6e6", "unit_id": "tag:072S:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "072S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$W \\xrightarrow{(E_W, f_W, 0_W)} \\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-Weierstrass-smooth-cover}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fb6316c3f385cf2d507d05eed06a499416892fcb4668a3e2ab5c4cfb6a611444", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b3155b12e5c8374d88273875e4a7fcab362bf4eb470c0c2f72397e8326fe6a52", "source_text": "The morphism <MATH_0001> is smooth\nand surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4b5855054f8a2b13ae641b7a6900ffaa688b24b988d818eb8c7afdd331de38b0", "unit_id": "tag:072T:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "math_text_regions": [{"delimiter_kind": "display-dollar", "pieces": [{"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0001"}, {"kind": "text", "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001"}, {"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0002"}, {"kind": "text", "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0002"}, {"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0003"}], "region_id": "math/0001", "slots": [{"boundary_placeholders": ["MATHSEG_0001", "MATHSEG_0002"], "classification_witness": {"anchor": {"file": "stacks-introduction.tex", "kind": "proof", "matches": [{"command_byte_span": {"end": 14299, "start": 14287}, "command_hash": "sha256:37729b561902acbfff7555a74bfedd302e33bb828af66514a619f6bed34f0143", "container_byte_span": {"end": 15201, "start": 13963}, "container_hash": "sha256:0dace7a69f9e96a18439f81086927c86e3d0011dc4ef339bc9fa4c36d65e0dda"}], "ordinal": 1, "owner_label": "stacks-introduction-lemma-Weierstrass-smooth-cover", "owner_tag": "072T", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14"}, "policy_hash": "sha256:878540b6cdbdc48efab8e6db8351e1c8fba4c3c4af0e4effe84233a954bb5508", "source_label": "stacks-introduction-lemma-Weierstrass-smooth-cover", "usage": "matrix-row-condition", "usage_source": {"after": " \\\\", "before": "u", "environments": ["matrix"]}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "stacks-introduction-unit", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 134, "start": 129}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001", "source": " unit"}, {"boundary_placeholders": ["MATHSEG_0002", "MATHSEG_0003"], "classification_witness": {"anchor": {"file": "stacks-introduction.tex", "kind": "proof", "matches": [{"command_byte_span": {"end": 14327, "start": 14310}, "command_hash": "sha256:b945a48cc86e4fdc27dc96a80768ee3825daf610eac859f9f6c945710f46e7e7", "container_byte_span": {"end": 15201, "start": 13963}, "container_hash": "sha256:0dace7a69f9e96a18439f81086927c86e3d0011dc4ef339bc9fa4c36d65e0dda"}], "ordinal": 1, "owner_label": "stacks-introduction-lemma-Weierstrass-smooth-cover", "owner_tag": "072T", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14"}, "policy_hash": "sha256:878540b6cdbdc48efab8e6db8351e1c8fba4c3c4af0e4effe84233a954bb5508", "source_label": "stacks-introduction-lemma-Weierstrass-smooth-cover", "usage": "matrix-row-condition", "usage_source": {"after": "\n\\end{matrix}", "before": "t", "environments": ["matrix"]}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "stacks-introduction-arbitrary", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 162, "start": 152}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0002", "source": " arbitrary"}], "source": "$$\nH =\n\\left\\{\n\\left(\n\\begin{matrix}\nu^2 & s & 0 \\\\\n0 & u^3 & 0 \\\\\nr & t & 1\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right)\n\\middle|\n\\begin{matrix}\nu\\text{ unit} \\\\\ns, r, t\\text{ arbitrary}\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}\n\\subset\n\\text{GL}_{3, \\mathbf{Z}}\n$$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 423, "start": 201}, "source_hash": "sha256:c33489dcbb972b4321115e3e0b929618973cc4f3e21b93d01562bf2962de07f3"}], "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "072S", "placeholders": {"MATHSEG_0001": "$$\nH =\n\\left\\{\n\\left(\n\\begin{matrix}\nu^2 & s & 0 \\\\\n0 & u^3 & 0 \\\\\nr & t & 1\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right)\n\\middle|\n\\begin{matrix}\nu\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "} \\\\\ns, r, t\\text{", "MATHSEG_0003": "}\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}\n\\subset\n\\text{GL}_{3, \\mathbf{Z}}\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$H \\times W \\to W$", "MATH_0002": "$H$", "MATH_0003": "$W$", "MATH_0004": "$H$", "MATH_0005": "$(E, f, 0)/S$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$(E, f, 0)$", "MATH_0008": "$H$", "MATH_0009": "$S \\times_{\\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}} W =\n\\mathit{Isom}_{S \\times W}(E \\times W, S \\times E_W)$", "MATH_0010": "$W \\to \\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}$", "MATH_0011": "$H$", "MATH_0012": "$H \\to \\Spec(\\mathbf{Z})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:83209b0cd07f0183819a55150617a9c6d3f840320696dc96436ae30d3d595a41", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:f6ab93ea06d657a210036fac384c00c8837c4b12956111db0f8fedf398624ca9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:aa876caf0663592d7bcb7876c26cb4907d177d9af3a03fd1438207b6e1d2b250", "source_text": "Surjectivity follows from the fact that every elliptic curve over a\nfield has a Weierstrass equation. We give a rough sketch of one\nway to prove smoothness. Consider the sub group scheme\n<MATHSEG_0001> unit<MATHSEG_0002> arbitrary<MATHSEG_0003>\nThere is an action <MATH_0001> of <MATH_0002> on the Weierstrass scheme <MATH_0003>.\nTo find the equations for this action write out what a coordinate change\ngiven by a matrix in <MATH_0004> does to the general Weierstrass equation.\nThen it turns out the following statements hold\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> any elliptic curve <MATH_0005> has Zariski locally on <MATH_0006>\na Weierstrass equation,\n<STRUCT_0003> any two Weierstrass equations for <MATH_0007> differ (Zariski locally)\nby an element of <MATH_0008>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nConsidering the fibre product\n<MATH_0009>\nwe conclude that this means that the morphism\n<MATH_0010> is an <MATH_0011>-torsor.\nSince <MATH_0012> is smooth, and since torsors\nover smooth group schemes are smooth we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0a61939b5e8b44a02fb09e1d0fde94f394bbd1f6b3310ce740d7302f9dbc86c8", "unit_id": "tag:072T:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "072S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{M}_{1, 1} = [W/H]$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\%"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-quotient-stack}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3296ac59d875b7cdc7f630b50c64da51d43c2897388becd54633f77a1cfe0cb7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0891ad2453879b02c3031fd23237cab026647d9e8464511bf01f0a1450ea1144", "source_text": "The argument sketched above actually shows that\n<MATH_0001> is a global quotient stack.\nIt is true about 50<STRUCT_0001> of the time that an argument proving a moduli\nstack is algebraic will show that it is a global quotient stack.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:54168bc4d99466a23d7be4c2fd81d6edf16bae85cf59609b024c37858aad267e", "unit_id": "tag:072U:statement"}
